# Discord LFG Bot - Project Structure

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

This is a Go-based Discord LFG (Looking for Group) bot that helps gamers form teams and manage voice channels automatically. The project follows standard Go project layout with clean architecture principles.

## 📁 Project Structure

```
discord-lfg-bot-go/
├── cmd/                           # Application entry points
│   ├── bot/main.go               # Main bot application
│   ├── migrate/                  # Database migration tool
│   └── example/                  # Example/test programs
├── internal/                     # Private application code
│   ├── bot/                      # Core bot logic and handlers
│   │   ├── bot.go               # Main bot struct and initialization
│   │   └── checkin_commands.go  # Check-in related commands
│   ├── achievement/              # Achievement system
│   ├── channel/                  # Discord channel management
│   ├── config/                   # Configuration loading and validation
│   ├── database/                 # Database operations and repository
│   ├── lottery/                  # Lottery/raffle system
│   ├── parser/                   # Message parsing logic
│   ├── role/                     # Discord role management
│   ├── team/                     # Team state management
│   └── temproom/                 # Temporary voice room management
├── pkg/                          # Public packages (reusable)
│   └── logger/                   # Logging utilities
├── config/                       # Configuration files
│   └── consise.env.example      # Environment template (copy to .env)
├── sql/                          # Database schemas and migrations
├── docker/                       # Docker configurations
├── docs/                         # Documentation
├── scripts/                      # Build and deployment scripts
├── logs/                         # Application logs
├── .cursor/rules/               # Cursor AI rules (this directory)
├── docker-compose.yml           # Development Docker setup
├── Makefile                     # Build automation
├── go.mod                       # Go module definition
└── README.md                    # Project documentation
```

## 🔧 Key Components

### Core Bot ([internal/bot/bot.go](mdc:internal/bot/bot.go))
- Main `Bot` struct with all dependencies
- Discord event handlers (message, voice state, member events)
- Graceful startup and shutdown
- Integration with all subsystems

### Message Parser ([internal/parser/](mdc:internal/parser/))
- Parses LFG messages in format: `游戏名 人数=当前人数`
- Game recognition by text-channel mapping (`CHANNEL_MAPPINGS` env var), not by name aliases
- Supports multiple formats: `5=1`, `1/5`, `（1/5）`

### Channel Manager ([internal/channel/](mdc:internal/channel/))
- Creates/manages temporary voice channels
- Channel naming: `[游戏名] 寻组 (当前人数/总人数)`
- Automatic cleanup after inactivity

### Team Manager ([internal/team/](mdc:internal/team/))
- Tracks team state and membership
- Handles team formation and completion
- Integrates with voice channel management

### Database Layer ([internal/database/](mdc:internal/database/))
- PostgreSQL for persistent data
- Redis for caching and session data
- Repository pattern for data access
- Connection pooling and health checks

### Configuration ([internal/config/](mdc:internal/config/) & [config/](mdc:config/))
- Environment-based configuration (all settings via `.env`)
- Feature flags support (temp rooms, LOL custom, dev cleanup)

## 🎮 Game System

Game-to-channel mappings are defined solely by the `CHANNEL_MAPPINGS` env var in `.env`:
- Format: `游戏名:文字频道ID:语音分类ID`, comma-separated
- The game is determined by which text channel the message was sent in
- Fallbacks: `DEFAULT_TEXT_CHANNEL_ID` / `DEFAULT_CATEGORY_ID`

## 🏛️ Architecture Patterns

### Clean Architecture
- **cmd/**: Application entry points
- **internal/**: Business logic (private to this app)
- **pkg/**: Reusable packages
- Clear separation of concerns

### Dependency Injection
```go
// Example from bot.go
bot := &Bot{
    session:            session,
    config:            cfg,
    teamManager:       team.NewManager(),
    channelManager:    channel.NewManager(session, cfg.GuildID, cfg),
    repository:        repo,
}
```

### Repository Pattern
```go
type Repository interface {
    GetUserByID(ctx context.Context, userID string) (*User, error)
    CreateTeam(ctx context.Context, team *Team) error
}
```

## 🛠️ Development Workflow

### Build System ([Makefile](mdc:Makefile))
- `make build`: Build the bot binary
- `make test`: Run all tests
- `make docker-build`: Build Docker image
- `make migrate`: Run database migrations

### Environment Setup
1. Copy `config/consise.env.example` to `.env`
2. Configure Discord token and channel IDs
3. Set up PostgreSQL and Redis
4. Run `make build && make run`

